    Law 2: a ground node under standing liquid reacts with the gas dissolved in it, renewed through the liquid's film
    
    A node's gas phase is the gas it touches. Under standing liquid (more than the
    pores hold) each gas it takes is held where the film (Flow's law, depth /
    dissolve) and its reactions balance: Henry's share x (1 + made tau/eq) /
    (1 + used tau/eq). No new number. The sea's salt balance and the worldgen start
    are unchanged (made = used at the balance). Runs, seeds 1-3, 64x64, 60 years:
    carbon gas 24-62 ppm lower at year 60, land dead matter +40-100% (wet land cells
    and the 6th order of reaction 21), books exact. Handover row, 6.1, 6.2, numbers.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

